--- body ---
## Context

`fetch.py:279` routes every ISBN to LibGen whatever `--source` says. LibGen is a shadow library behind
the opt-in `shadow` extra, so a default install cannot fetch any book. DOAB (Directory of Open Access
Books) and OAPEN list open-access books with PDFs and are searchable by ISBN. Many books also carry a
Crossref DOI, which already takes the DOI path.

New capability: the author confirmed it on 2026-10-29.

## Actions
1. A `doab` source under 0008's contract: `ACCEPTS` holds ISBN; it looks the ISBN up in DOAB/OAPEN and
   downloads the open-access PDF when one is listed.
2. ISBN dispatch goes through `ACCEPTS` like every other kind: drop the LibGen special case. The
   default cascade for ISBNs is the open source(s) only; LibGen runs only when selected explicitly,
   consistent with the open-plus-institutional default (0008 log).
3. README: books are fetched from DOAB by default, LibGen opt-in.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] An open-access book is fetched by ISBN on a default install (no extras)
- [ ] No ISBN special case left in the CLI dispatch
- [ ] Conformance suite (0009) covers the new source
